  "notes": "Modified cash basis audit, FYE 9/30/2022 (same structure as FY2023). Governmental lines from the Statement of Revenues, Expenditures, and Changes in Fund Balances (Total column, p4); no transfers printed. Fund balances 127,266 -> 32,620 (127,266 + 152,696 - 247,342 = 32,620); ending cash = Cash + Cash at county treasurer from the governmental funds balance sheet (p3), CDs 18,233 as investments; no beginning cash printed. Business-type (Water, Sewer) receipts/disbursements and balances from the proprietary Statement of Cash Flows - Modified Cash Basis (p7, Total column), measure cash, as FY2023: 73,907 + 177,268 - 150,377 = 100,798. Proprietary cash flow statement left null as in FY2023/FY2024 (operating 27,156, capital and related financing -51,333, investing 51,068, p7). Business-type detail per fund from the proprietary revenues/expenses statement (p6); utility 'Miscellaneous' operating revenue is counted in Charges for Services by the Statement of Activities (p2), so charges for services. Balance sheet = government-wide Statement of Net Position (p1), because the governmental funds balance sheet (42,726) does not equal the governmental activities figures (capital assets). The only supplementary schedule is the combined all-funds budget-and-actual statement (p9: receipts 329,964, disbursements 393,568, broad groups Taxes/State/Local), so detail is one line per fund column of the governmental funds statement (General, Street) and the proprietary funds statement (Water, Sewer). Read pages 1-9 of 9"
